<title>BELGIUM: Clabecq will not be suspended - bourse.</title>
<headline>Clabecq will not be suspended - bourse.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade in shares of Belgian steel maker Forges de Clabecq will not be suspended following news that the European Union plans to rule against a state aid plan for Clabecq, a Brussels bourse official said on Monday.</p>
<p>The European Commission said earlier it plans to rule next week that a 1.5 billion franc captial injection for the steel maker amounts to public subsidies and cannot be approved.</p>
<p>Clabecq is traded on the Brussels bourse's cash market, where share prices are fixed twice a day. The share closed at 175 francs on Friday.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
